# Shared EA feature sets this board pulls in. One word per feature, space
# separated. Each lives in board/ea-common/features/<name>/, holding both its
# halves: defconfig (userspace) and linux.fragment (kernel).
#   wifi  - Atheros ath9k radio + wpa_supplicant/iw userspace
#   emmc  - sdhci-pci + ext4, persistent rootfs on mmcblk0p1
#   switch - BCM53125 managed switch over SPI (DSA/b53); gives lan1/lan2
wifi emmc

# TEMPORARILY reduced from `wifi emmc switch audio` (2026-08-31), same reason as
# ea3-v2 -- see TEMPORARILY-DISABLED.md at the repo root.
#
# `switch` and `audio` are both written =y and would overrun CEFDK's
# 7,417,856-byte bootlinux window, which an x86_64 kernel already fills to
# 7,037,952. An oversized kernel is TRUNCATED silently and simply does not boot.
# Bring them back as modules (=m), not built in.
#
# `wifi` is KEPT, because this is the EA-3 variant that has a radio and the AP +
# captive portal is how an unplugged unit is set up. It is affordable now only
# because the wifi feature's linux.fragment builds ath9k/mac80211/cfg80211 as
# MODULES; as =y they were about a megabyte and did not fit either.
